{"title":"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Gaussville's soccer team won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e4e5c6d549ce47918b94180cad5c1644d9ea88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of their first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> games. They went on to win <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> games in a row. At this point, they had won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the total games they had played. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b744040da3313f2445c3ba94d5eddb31b2f7f2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 10 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 12 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since they won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e4e5c6d549ce47918b94180cad5c1644d9ea88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of their first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> games before winning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> more, they had won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f5118d0c36ab400df21f4d5dcd04b106ff91ba63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\% \\times 40 + n = n + \\frac{4}{10} \\times 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"229\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/415507b7cde68c0e553982cd5b16b3128f200a34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> games in total.\n</p><p>There would also be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/eba868fd6659be6412874a2d8ec4c025fc395369.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> games.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of some number is equal to half of that number. This means that because they won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of their games after winning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> more games:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/f/37fb352f145d5a1f92db2624ef65be25778264a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(n + 16) = n + 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/f/5ff7cb7a68aa5cfe0c514f2bb515a2d1e444c0e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times n + 2 \\times 16 = n + 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/3/f33f4c42c559057ec2a3aa3850b5e1cd128c5cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n + 32 = n + 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594fb716693453e3c3b7c1a1678a1de79e5837ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n - n = 40 - 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75b73f2c57b033f328868053398c8bf7e46bc7de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"93\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 1, we see that the team won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/415507b7cde68c0e553982cd5b16b3128f200a34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> games in total but had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> games won at first. However, they would have had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/2/d22d04e0708cdd91e94ccfbb7640e6f067b19c48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40 - 16 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"101\" height=\"13\" /> losses and draws in total since there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> games at the start. Because half the number of games were wins at the end, the same number of games would have been either losses or draws as wins, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0ee3f9905dfa61b551b2177ff25b61da731ffd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 16 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/248c52c15d8cc8dbf5691a7143a7c9291078c81e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 24 - 16 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"176\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\"